From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xylar Asay-Davis <xylarstorm@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:16:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Export an include directory that exists

The exported aziotsharedutil target advertised
${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/azureiot as its public include directory, but
that directory is only created by the install(FILES ...) rule on the line
below, whose file lists (micromock_h_files_full_path, INSTALL_H_FILES) are
empty unless the test targets are configured. install(FILES) with an empty
list installs nothing and creates no directory, so the exported target
referenced a path the package does not ship and downstream
find_package(azure_c_shared_utility CONFIG) users failed at CMake's generate
step.

The public headers are installed to ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/azure_c_shared_utility
and are included as "azure_c_shared_utility/xlogging.h", so the directory
that belongs on the include path is ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR} itself.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index bb100c7..2737fa4 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -699,7 +699,7 @@ install (TARGETS ${targets} EXPORT aziotsharedutilTargets
     LIBRARY DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}
     ARCHIVE DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}
     RUNTIME DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR}
-    INCLUDES DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/azureiot
+    INCLUDES DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}
 )
 install (FILES ${source_h_files} DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/azure_c_shared_utility)
 install (FILES ${micromock_h_files_full_path} ${INSTALL_H_FILES} DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/azureiot)
